alex: Quick Q on SSO/SCIM — users removed from Okta groups aren't getting deprovisioned in Redwood. SAML assertions show groups removed, SCIM logs show a PATCH but DB still has the group. @mira can you take a look? Here's the SCIM payload we captured (redacted emails):
```PATCH /Users/123
{
  "schemas": ["urn:ietf:params:scim:api:messages:2.0:PatchOp"],
  "Operations": [{
    "op": "remove",
    "path": "groups[value eq "eng-team"]"
  }]
}
```
Also seeing audit id a1b2c3 in the logs. Any privacy/redaction concerns if I paste full logs here?

mira: short version — probably a group-mapping mismatch. Okta sometimes sends group in "display" or as an "externalId" depending on mapping. Our SCIM handler currently checks group.value == externalId, so if Okta pushed display we ignore. Mask emails before pasting logs (use hashed ids). Send the app mapping screenshot (mask account emails) and I'll confirm.

sam: FYI I flipped the app to "Push groups" yesterday but the sync schedule was set to 12h. For push events Okta sometimes issues "replace" with an empty members array instead of explicit "remove". Our handler must treat both "remove" and "replace[] empty" as removals.

jen: I opened an access approval for ops to inspect user records: https://internal/approvals/PR-4567 — approvers @mira @jen. I'll also queue a tiny hotfix to treat replace-with-empty like remove and roll to staging.

security-bot: AUDIT: scim.event a1b2c3 for user:123 - op=PATCH - masked_email=***@redacted - ts=1749801300 - action=queued-for-review (automated)

alex: Thanks. One more: are we allowed to log full SAML assertions in debug? Policy seemed strict. Can I log assertion IDs and group names (non-email) and hash emails? Confirm before I paste anything into the thread.

mira: Policy = do not store raw SAML assertions. You may persist extracted attributes (group names, nameIDs) but emails must be hashed/truncated. Recommended approach: store sha256(email) and keep first 8 hex chars + "..." or use an internal opaque id. Also add a short note in the SCIM debugging docs about redaction.

sam: I'll add a small middleware to redact emails from SCIM logs and to normalize group ops. Pseudo:```js
req.body.Operations.forEach(op => {
  if(op.path && op.path.includes('groups')) normalizeGroupOp(op)
  if(op.value && looksLikeEmail(op.value)) op.value = hash8(op.value)
})
``` Will test in staging and attach logs (masked).

alex: Awesome, thanks team :thumbsup:
